From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: port <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 18 Sep 2026 22:28:45 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] rename the i2c driver to ecam25_ar0234

JetPack 7 ships its own nv_ar0234.ko for the Leopard Hawk module, whose
i2c_driver is also named ar0234. Two i2c drivers with one name collide in sysfs
and the second registration returns -EEXIST. The of_match compatible stays
nvidia,ar0234, so the device tree binding is unchanged.

The v4l2 subdev name follows the driver name, so it becomes
'ecam25_ar0234 <bus>-0042'. The devname property in the overlay's
tegra-camera-platform node has to match.
---
 ar0234.c | 4 ++--
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/ar0234.c b/ar0234.c
index d7e1661..31c244a 100644
--- a/ar0234.c
+++ b/ar0234.c
@@ -3177,7 +3177,7 @@ static void cam_remove(struct i2c_client *client)
 }
 
 static const struct i2c_device_id cam_id[] = {
-	{"ar0234", 0},
+	{"ecam25_ar0234", 0},
 	{}
 };
 
@@ -3185,7 +3185,7 @@ MODULE_DEVICE_TABLE(i2c, cam_id);
 
 static struct i2c_driver cam_i2c_driver = {
 	.driver = {
-		   .name = "ar0234",
+		   .name = "ecam25_ar0234",
 		   .owner = THIS_MODULE,
 		   .of_match_table = of_match_ptr(cam_of_match),
 		   },
